kedu.guide.usage.title=Guidebook - How to use
kedu.guide.usage.header=Basic flow
kedu.guide.usage.body=Camouflage a shape\n1. Place an untextured Camo shape.\n2. Hold a compatible Vanilla block.\n3. Interact with the shape to copy the look.\n\nRemove a texture\n1. Hold the Camo Scraper.\n2. Aim at a textured Camo shape.\n3. Interact to restore the wooden frame.\n\nNotes\nThe source block is not consumed. A Camo shape drops only the addon block.
kedu.guide.camo.title=Guidebook - Camo Blocks
kedu.guide.camo.header=Camouflage shapes
kedu.guide.camo.body=Main shapes\n- Full block\n- Pass-through block with no collision\n- Stair with automatic corners\n- Bottom, top and double slab\n- Vertical slab on four sides\n- Connectable fence\n- Connectable wall\n- Bottom or top trapdoor\n\nPlacement tip\nAim high on a side, or click the lower face of another block, to place some shapes in the upper half. Aim low, or click the top face, for the lower half.
kedu.guide.special.title=Guidebook - Special blocks
kedu.guide.special.header=Special blocks
kedu.guide.special.body=Pass-through block\nCollisionless Camo shape. Use it for hidden entrances and passable details.\n\nCloud Block\nCreated by Cloud in a Bucket. It is temporary, collisionless, translucent and disappears after about 5 seconds.\n\nVisual feedback\nTools use a short black and yellow particle to indicate targets and preview positions.
kedu.guide.shapes.title=Guidebook - Shapes
kedu.guide.shapes.header=Available shapes
kedu.guide.shapes.body=• Full block\n• Pass-through full block with no collision, intended for hidden entrances\n• Stairs with automatic inner and outer corners\n• Bottom, top and double slabs\n• Vertical slabs on all four sides\n• Connectable wooden fence\n• Connectable stone wall\n• Rotatable bottom/top trapdoors with open and close sounds\n\nAim at the upper half of a side or click the underside of another block to place slabs and trapdoors in the top half. Aim lower or click the top face for the bottom half. Stairs corner across all Camo texture banks.
kedu.guide.scraper.title=Guidebook - Tool
kedu.guide.scraper.header=Camo Scraper
kedu.guide.scraper.body=Use\nHold the Scraper and aim at a textured Camo shape. The outline shows the texture can be removed. Interact to restore the wooden frame.\n\nTip\nTo replace a texture, remove the current texture and apply another compatible block.
kedu.guide.crafting.title=Guidebook - Crafting
kedu.guide.crafting.header=Real recipes
kedu.guide.crafting.body=Legend: C=Copper, R=Redstone, S=Stick, B=Bucket, P=Membrane, N=Snowball, F=Feather, E=Ender Pearl, I=Iron, M=Compass, T=String, H=Piston, W=Tagged wood.\n\nCamo Block\n[S] [S] [S]\n[S] [W] [S]\n[S] [S] [S]\n-> 8 Camo Blocks\nW accepts minecraft:planks, minecraft:logs, minecraft:crimson_stems, minecraft:warped_stems or minecraft:wooden_slabs. Wood from other addons works when it uses one of these standard tags.\n\nCopper Wrench\n[ ] [C] [ ]\n[C] [M] [C]\n[ ] [S] [ ]\n-> 1 Copper Wrench\n\nTexture Trowel\n[C] [R] [C]\n[ ] [I] [ ]\n[ ] [S] [ ]\n-> 1 Texture Trowel\n\nMeasuring Tape\n[ ] [T] [C]\n[T] [R] [ ]\n[C] [ ] [ ]\n-> 1 Measuring Tape\n\nCloud in a Bucket\n[N] [P] [N]\n[N] [B] [N]\n[ ] [N] [ ]\n-> 1 Cloud in a Bucket\n\nBlock Repositioner\n[H] [E] [H]\n[ ] [C] [ ]\n[ ] [S] [ ]\n-> 1 Repositioner\n\nContext Brush\n[ ] [F] [F]\n[ ] [C] [F]\n[S] [ ] [ ]\n-> 1 Brush\n\nThese grids match the Behavior Pack recipe files.
kedu.guide.tools.title=Guidebook - Tools
kedu.guide.tools.header=Building tools
kedu.guide.tools.body=Tools use sounds and particles for common actions. Chat is reserved for measurements and important errors.\n\nCreative has no item consumption or durability damage. In Survival, tools may lose durability and some actions consume blocks.
kedu.guide.measure.title=Guidebook - Measuring Tape
kedu.guide.measure.header=Measure two points
kedu.guide.measure.body=Purpose\nMeasures two points in the world.\n\nHow to use\n1. Interact with the first block to mark point A.\n2. The particle stays on point A while you look for point B.\n3. Interact with the second block to finish.\n\nResult\nChat shows distance, X/Y/Z difference and region size.
kedu.guide.wrench.title=Guidebook - Copper Wrench
kedu.guide.wrench.header=Safe state-based rotation
kedu.guide.wrench.body=Purpose\nRotates blocks with direction, axis, face or vertical-half states.\n\nHow to use\nHold the Copper Wrench and aim at a supported block. The particle shows that the block can rotate. Interact to rotate.\n\nSupports\nStairs, pistons, compatible Camo shapes, logs, signs and other blocks with rotation states. If no supported state exists, nothing changes.
kedu.guide.trowel.title=Guidebook - Texture Trowel
kedu.guide.trowel.header=Random hotbar palette
kedu.guide.trowel.body=Purpose\nPlaces random blocks using valid hotbar materials.\n\nHow to use\nAim at a block face. The particle shows the adjacent position where the new block will be placed. Interact to place one random hotbar material.\n\nImportant\nThe Trowel does not replace the aimed block. Survival consumes 1 block of the chosen material. Creative consumes nothing.
kedu.guide.brush.title=Guidebook - Context Brush
kedu.guide.brush.header=Contextual replacement
kedu.guide.brush.body=Purpose\nReplaces a block with the most common nearby material.\n\nHow to use\nInteract with the target. The tool checks the six direct neighbors and applies the most frequent type.\n\nSurvival\nConsumes 1 matching block and returns the replaced block when safe. Containers and technical blocks are blocked.
kedu.guide.mover.title=Guidebook - Block Repositioner
kedu.guide.mover.header=Move without duplication
kedu.guide.mover.body=Purpose\nMoves a safe block without duplicating it.\n\nHow to use\n1. Interact with the source block.\n2. The particle marks the source.\n3. Interact with the face where the block should appear.\n\nLimits\nEmpty destination, same dimension and up to 16 blocks on each axis. Sneak and interact to cancel. Blocks with inventories or own data are blocked.
kedu.guide.cloud.title=Guidebook - Cloud in a Bucket
kedu.guide.cloud.header=Cloud building
kedu.guide.cloud.body=Purpose\nCreates a temporary block in the air to help building.\n\nHow to use\nHold Cloud in a Bucket and aim at a valid position. The particle shows exactly where the cloud will appear. Use the item to place it.\n\nDetails\nThe cloud has no collision, lets light pass and disappears after about 5 seconds. In Survival the tool loses durability.
